  "body": "### Description\n\nMatrix-synapse installed from package on Ubuntu 11. Server placed in isolated LAN without Internet connection. Internal DNS configured and workable\r\nElement client allows me to register my username and password. I am able to chat, sent emoji, make audio and video calls.\r\nI cannot post any file to the room from Android client. It shows, that file uploading in a progress but never finished.\r\nFrom windows Element client I am able to post files to the same room.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Setup matrix-synapse on the LAN not connected to the Internet\r\n2. Open any chat on Android\r\n3. Upload any file or make photo or record short message\r\n4. File cannot be uploaded\r\n\n\n### Homeserver\n\nmatrix.protected.local\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n{\"server\":{\"name\":\"Synapse\",\"version\":\"1.86.0\"}}\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDocker (matrixdotorg/synapse)\n\n### Database\n\nSQLite\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nDebian 11 + docker + Synapse as a container + nginx proxy\n\n### Configuration\n\nenable_registration: true\r\nenable_registration_without_verification: true\r\ntrusted_key_servers: []\r\nfederation_domain_whitelist:\r\nmax_upload_size: 50M\r\n\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nI am not sure how to collect logs on docker.\r\nMy logs when I try Synapse from package don't show any errors.\r\nOn docker I cannot even find logs. Please advise how to collect it.\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
